library "Semnot Refuse 232".

// A NON-truth-set operand under a NO-BASE sem-not has no complement universe →
// must LOUD-REFUSE (hardError + compile-failing sentinel), never silently emit
// the operand unnegated. This single-library `coded from` policy resolves through
// the off-lane, whose operand flavor is unmodeled (`unknown`); a layered
// RecordSource operand would classify `resource-list` — both refuse identically.
terminology "Virtual Encounter Class":
- valueset is `http://example.org/crl/ValueSet/virtual-encounter`.

concept "Virtual Encounters":
- type is Encounter.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- coded from "Virtual Encounter Class".

concept "Not Virtual (standalone)":
- type is Encounter.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- defined as ( sem-not "Virtual Encounters" ).
